# SLIC Alpha

MATLAB source code for five whole-brain parcellation approaches operating on resting-state fMRI data.

[GPL-3.0 license](LICENSE)

The methods include three normalized-cut-based approaches and two approaches combining normalized cuts with SLIC. The original documentation describes this repository as source code to customize for a specific dataset.

## Getting Started

Review [parc_main.m](parc_main.m) as the processing outline before running an experiment.

- Prepare MATLAB with Parallel Computing Toolbox and the NIfTI functions `load_untouch_nii` and `save_untouch_nii` on the path.
- Supply preprocessed images as `data/subNNNNN.nii`, matching the subject identifiers in `sSub.mat`.
- Review the included parameter files and gray-matter mask for your dataset.
- Adapt the hardcoded subject count, cluster-count loop, group repetitions, and parallel-worker settings in `parc_main.m`.

## Known Incomplete Steps

The final evaluation section of [parc_main.m](parc_main.m) calls `eval_dice_MSC_sub` and `eval_dice_SLIC_sub`, but neither function is present in the tracked repository. Resolve those dependencies before treating the complete script as runnable.

The script is therefore a starting point for a configured research workflow, rather than a verified one-command demo.

## Repository Structure

- [parc_main.m](parc_main.m): processing and evaluation outline.
- [parc_preprocess.m](parc_preprocess.m): subject-image preparation.
- [SLIC.m](SLIC.m), [SLIC_mean_parc.m](SLIC_mean_parc.m), and [SLIC_twolevel_parc.m](SLIC_twolevel_parc.m): SLIC-related methods.
- [MSC_mean_parc.m](MSC_mean_parc.m), [MSC_twolevel_parc.m](MSC_twolevel_parc.m), and [MKSC_parc.m](MKSC_parc.m): other parcellation methods.
- [sSub.mat](sSub.mat), [sK.mat](sK.mat), and `randset_*.mat`: bundled experiment configuration.
- [graymatter.nii](graymatter.nii) and [T1_4mm.nii](T1_4mm.nii): image resources.

## Related Projects

- [SLIC on NITRC](https://www.nitrc.org/projects/slic/): project link preserved from the original documentation.

